# Build context control.
#
# Without this file the context is ~6.6 GB - the virtualenv, the local avatar
# assets and the git history - all of which is uploaded to the remote builder
# on every deploy and none of which the image uses. The Dockerfile copies
# pyproject.toml, uv.lock, src/, infra/piper/server.py and the entrypoint;
# everything else here is noise or, in the case of .env, a credential that
# must never enter a build context at all.

.venv/
assets/
.git/
.github/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db

# Real credentials. Never copied by the Dockerfile, excluded here as well so a
# future COPY cannot pick them up by accident.
.env
.env.local

docs/
tests/
apps/
.DS_Store
